  "domain": "tier0/export/processing",
  "description": "Item 2.1 (phase3.1_export-island-padding) seam-end overhang sweep, exploratory: which far texel window along the seam Painter takes for a ring texel past a seam end, as the far point moves along the seam across a far texel centre (decision 275's window boundary). 510 copies of export-padding-fold-tie's ratio-1 seam pair (A and B 4 x 4 texels, separate UV islands, B at turn 0, A 0.25 texel and the far point 0.625 texel off the grid across the seam) folded convex flat, 90 degrees and along the Pythagorean directions 12-5-13, 4-3-5, 3-4-5 and 5-12-13, at c 2^-k cm per texel; the ring row above A's top seam end 0.5 to 0.75 texel past it in 1/16 steps; the far point -1/8 to +1/8 texel along the seam from a far texel centre in 1/64 steps; every position and UV exact in float32, mesh box exactly [-256, 256] cm in x and z and [-64, 64] in y; each copy its own 3D piece; document resolution 512. User0-User7 added as RGB32F (a record whose template capture shows one of them not 32F is void); one fill with the eight channels active, Normal at opacity 1, default projection (read back), sources the authored float32 kernel code at the document size: User0-User2 one-hot the nine classes x mod 3 + 3 (y mod 3) of the texel (column x, row y from the top), User3 the UV ramp R = (x + 0.5)/N, G = (y + 0.5)/N, B = 0.5, User4 and User5 the periodic codes d and e (k/256, one 17 x 13 texel tile each), User6 (d + e)/2 and User7 1 - d. The eight maps at OpenEXR 32f with infinite padding and with passthrough (every covered texel must equal its source bit for bit, or the probe is void), every export step done twice in the session.",
